.TH LEGION-CONTROL 1 "2026-08-11" "Legion Control 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
legion-control \- native controls for the supported Lenovo Legion 83LU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B legion-control
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B legion-control
starts the unprivileged GTK4 interface. Hardware mutations are delegated to a
fixed PolicyKit helper. The current mutation allowlist contains only Lenovo DMI
product 83LU (Legion Pro 5 16IAX10H).
.PP
The application controls platform profiles, validated fan modes, bounded Custom
CPU power, selected device switches, and the exact ITE 048d:c195 24-zone RGB
keyboard endpoint. It installs no DKMS module and performs no network access.
.SH SAFETY
Do not bypass product or controller checks. At 98 degrees Celsius, or when no
trustworthy temperature is available, the fan daemon returns control to
firmware. Package removal also attempts restoration.
.PP
If cooling is uncertain, stop heavy work and use the application's return-to-
firmware action before collecting diagnostics.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/legion-control/fan-config.json
Root-owned active fan policy.
.TP
.I /var/lib/legion-control/rgb-config.json
Last RGB configuration accepted by the helper; not semantic hardware readback.
.TP
.I ~/.config/legion-control/scenes.json
User-owned quick scenes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
